"},{"identifier":"C","content":"4f<sup>7</sup>5d<sup>1</sup>6s<sup>2</sup>"},{"identifier":"D","content":"4f<sup>3</sup>5d<sup>5</sup>6s<sup>2</sup>"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Electronic configuration of Gd(64) : [Xe]4f<sup>7</sup>5s<sup>2</sup>5p<sup>6</sup>5d<sup>1</sup>6s<sup>2</sup>\n<br><br>So the outer electronic configuration will be : 4f<sup>7</sup>5d<sup>1</sup>6s<sup>2</sup>\n<br><br><b>Shortcut Method :</b> Gd belongs to 4f series which is also called lanthanide series. In this lanthanide series for Cerium (Ce), Gadolinium (Gd) and Lutetium (Lu) outer d orbital has 1 electron and for all other lanthanide series elements outer d orbital has 0 electron. From this you can easily say option (C) is correct."}},"permalink":"outer-electronic-configuration-of-gd-atomic-no-64-is-2011-marks-4-1lgri6pkbemtwbzp.htm","timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2011","topic":"periodic-table-and-its-features","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"aieee-2011","active":true}],"ids":["6sdOsvsLIgW18g66","RoaWGv7xoIOnOfUP","4ECfPwwyPWONuD2m","1lgrI6PKBEmtwbZP"],"title":"AIEEE 2011 | JEE Main Year Wise Previous Years Questions","canonical":"https://app/past-years/jee/silver-mirror-test-is-given-by-which-one-of-the-following-co-2011-marks-4-6sdosvsligw18g66.htm"}